A dog barks outside my door.
I open it, and Nina stands there with her dog, Ludwig.
He wags his tail and runs straight into my apartment.
"Welcome, little friend," I say to him.
Nina smiles and gives me a bag with his things.
"Thank you very much for the help this weekend," she says.
She takes his dry food and a leash out of the bag.
"You must give him food twice a day," Nina explains.
"Give it to him in the red bowl."
I nod and put the bag on the table.
"May I give him a treat later?" I ask her.
"No, he definitely must not have our food," she answers.
"Only give him his own food."
She then points at the leash.
"And remember the traffic outside," she says seriously.
"You must always keep him on a leash close to the road."
"Keep him close to you."
I promise to look after him really well.
Nina hugs me and says goodbye to Ludwig.
Now the two of us are ready for a lovely weekend together.
